          "guid": "mszggv7xtlf43q6s",
          "message": {
            "text": "The result mapping keys on typeof value === 'string', not truthiness — so an empty string is a valid OK result, distinct from null dismissal.\n\nprompt() resolves three distinct DOM outcomes onto two logical ones: OK → close(value) (a string, possibly ''), Cancel → close(null), and Escape/backdrop dismissal → the overlay's default close(undefined). Mapping typeof value === 'string' ? value : null collapses both cancel and dismissal to null while preserving '' as a genuine result. A truthiness check (value || null) would be wrong here: it would turn a user who cleared the field and pressed OK into a null, indistinguishable from cancel. The unit test \"an empty string is a valid OK result (not null)\" pins exactly this. form() uses the analogous value !== null && typeof value === 'object' guard for the same reason — a {} record from an all-empty form is still a submit, not a cancel.\n",
            "markdown": "The result mapping keys on `typeof value === 'string'`, not truthiness — so an empty string is a valid OK result, distinct from `null` dismissal.\n\n`prompt()` resolves three distinct DOM outcomes onto two logical ones: OK → `close(value)` (a string, possibly `''`), Cancel → `close(null)`, and Escape/backdrop dismissal → the overlay's default `close(undefined)`. Mapping `typeof value === 'string' ? value : null` collapses both cancel and dismissal to `null` while preserving `''` as a genuine result. A truthiness check (`value || null`) would be wrong here: it would turn a user who cleared the field and pressed OK into a `null`, indistinguishable from cancel. The unit test \"an empty string is a valid OK result (not null)\" pins exactly this. `form()` uses the analogous `value !== null && typeof value === 'object'` guard for the same reason — a `{}` record from an all-empty form is still a submit, not a cancel.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/overlay.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 394,
                  "endLine": 394,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  return handle.result.then((value) => (typeof value === 'string' ? value : null));"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
